1
00:00:00,130 --> 00:00:06,899
Open hardware. Open software. Reinforcement learning on a stock ESP32.

2
00:00:07,330 --> 00:00:12,099
Meet Rider2-RL. A wheeled robot for just over four hundred US dollars.

3
00:00:13,130 --> 00:00:19,053
Train the balance policy in MuJoCo, on a laptop CPU. No GPU needed.

4
00:00:20,330 --> 00:00:25,945
Just one thousand, seven hundred and ninety-six parameters. About seven kilobytes of weights.

5
00:00:26,530 --> 00:00:30,607
Export to native C plus plus. No inference framework on the robot.

6
00:00:31,530 --> 00:00:34,299
A lift guard suppresses wheel runaway when picked up.

7
00:00:36,730 --> 00:00:39,730
Free-fall detection triggers a stop and releases servo torque.

8
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:49,761
Now open source on GitHub. Get the code, train your own policy, and build on ESP32.
